                <pb facs="0471" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/55: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Maginnis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-17T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1920—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>45. Your July 12, 6 p.m.</p>
                <p>The Department desires you to keep it fully and closely informed of all
                    developments in the situation, particularly those affecting the foreign policy
                    of the Government now in control. You are instructed to take no action which
                    could be construed as constituting recognition of the Provisional Government by
                    the Government of the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
